Source preservation and separate TeX styles

The 68 and 26 files originally imported in commit
bc00be012f7155e0024e1cb15a83bb1c2498b18f match their respective arXiv source
archives byte-for-byte, checked on 13 October 2026. Tekai has not changed
those paper files. This notice and distribution-source additions are separate
from the original archives. Retain the original file headers and notices.

The LeJEPA fixture includes Patrick W. Daly's natbib 8.31 and Piet van
Oostrum's fancyhdr 3.2 under the LaTeX Project Public License, version 1 or
later, as stated in their file headers. The paper's Creative Commons grant
does not replace those terms. natbib-8.31-sources.tar.gz contains natbib.dtx
and the matching package distribution required by the generated natbib.sty's
notice. See natbib-8.31-SOURCE for provenance and file hashes. Keeping this
source package archived prevents its older bibliography styles from shadowing
the bundled styles during fixture compilation. Other included styles retain
their original
attribution and any file-specific terms, including the NeurIPS style credits
to Roman Garnett and the earlier nips15submit_e.sty contributors.
